NVIDIA OptiX

Umbra traces rays on NVIDIA GPUs with OptiX 9.0, which the NVIDIA driver
provides at run time. Umbra includes no OptiX file and needs no OptiX SDK
to build. Most of the SDK's headers are licensed under NVIDIA's proprietary
DesignWorks SDK agreement, which does not allow redistribution under an
open-source license, so none of their text is copied.

These files are written by hand and hold only the interoperability facts of
OptiX's ABI that Umbra uses, which Umbra's MIT License covers as far as
they are Umbra's own work: the names and operands of the `_optix_*` device
built-ins, the slot order of the host function table of ABI version 105,
the layout of the structs passed to it, and their constants.

-   crates/umbra-kernels/src/optix.rs: the device API, in inline PTX.
-   crates/umbra-gpu/src/optix/ffi.rs: the host function table and types.

